          "evaluationDate": "2026-02-23T00:00:00.0Z",
          "reason": "Carlos Rivera, biweekly, L2 Apex.Benefits monthly transit election $400. IRC §132(f) monthly limit $340 (lookup US.FederalTaxParameters.TransitMonthlyLimit, Rev. Proc. 2025-32). Pre-tax part WT 1250 = $340 × 12 / 26 = $156.92; excess WT 5520 (post-tax) = $60 × 12 / 26 = $27.69. FIT/FICA taxable = $7,115.38 - $156.92 = $6,958.46 (WT 5050/5051). FIT (WT 5100, Pub 15-T Worksheet 1A, Single): $6,958.46 × 26 = $180,919.96 - Step 1g $8,600 = $172,319.96 → $17,966 + 24% × ($172,319.96 - $113,200) = $32,154.79/yr ÷ 26 = $1,236.72. SS 6.2% × $6,958.46 = $431.42. Medicare 1.45% × $6,958.46 = $100.90. State withholding (WT 5310): NY and CT exclude the transit salary reduction (wages $6,958.46), NJ taxes it (wages $7,115.38, N.J.S.A. 54A:6-23.c; TB-24(R)). NJ nonresident on the NJ wages 25%: NJ-W4 single (status S), rate A $7,115.38 × 25% = $1,778.85 → $31 + ($1,778.85 - $1,538) × 6.1% = $45.69. CT nonresident on all CT wages × 15%: CT-W4 code F (TPG-211 2026, annualized $180,919.96: exemption $0, tax $4,750 + 6% × ($180,919.96 - $100,000) = $9,605.20, phase-out add-back $250, recapture $250, credit 0%) → $10,105.20 ÷ 26 = $388.66 × 15% = $58.30. NY resident on all NY wages (IT-2104 single, 0 allowances): $6,958.46 - $284.60 = $6,673.86 → $372.04 + ($6,673.86 - $6,063) × 6.4% = $411.14, minus NJ and CT withholding: $411.14 - $45.69 - $58.30 = $307.15. WT 5310 = $45.69 + $58.30 + $307.15 = $411.14. NY PFL (WT 5620): 0.432% × $6,958.46 = $30.06. Net = $7,115.38 - $156.92 - $27.69 - $1,236.72 - $431.42 - $100.90 - $411.14 - $30.06 = $4,720.53. Validates the T4-Customizing L2 regulation without modifying the base US.Payroll regulation.",
